## 1. What the engine actually runs (read from the code, not the README)

The repository serves DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (not V3/R1) on Blackwell Ultra:

| item | value | where it comes from |
|---|---|---|
| model | **DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash**: 40-layer Causal Encoder-Decoder (20 + 20), multimodal, {{ (w.param_counts.backbone_total/1e9)|n(0) }}B backbone + {{ (w.param_counts.engram_tables/1e9)|n(1) }}B Engram parameters | `crates/model/src/config.rs`, HF `config.json` |
| hardware | 4 x GB300 (TP4) or 8 x B300 (TP8), `sm_103a` | README |
| batch | **one request at a time**: the server holds a single `Job` that every rank executes | `crates/server/src/engine.rs` (`Shared.job`, `next_job`) |
| parallelism | pure tensor parallelism. Query heads, `wo_a` groups, `wo_b` rows, the vocab, **and every routed/shared expert by its intermediate dim** (2304/TP) are sharded. `wq_a`+`wkv`, the indexer `wq_b`, compressor, gate and mHC projections are **replicated**. There is no expert parallelism and no all-to-all: two all-reduces per layer, fused with the mHC epilogue (NVLS / Lamport buffers) | `crates/engine/src/weights.rs::layer`, `model.rs::comm_ex`, `cu/comm.cu` |
| speculation | DSpark: 3 drafter blocks (SWA-only attention, 128-expert top-3 MoE) draft 5 tokens; the backbone verifies **6 rows** per step (adaptive length via a CUDA-graph conditional switch) | `model.rs::capture_spec_blk`, `capture_spec_vadapt` |
| weights | routed experts **FP4 E2M1** with an E8M0 scale per 32 (stored as packed `I8`), dense projections **FP8 E4M3** with E8M0 per 32x32 block, head **BF16** (an FP8 copy is used for drafting, and for verify on GB300 TP4). In memory each rank's slice is padded to 128 rows, but the routed-expert tensor maps read only the real rows plus w2's 64-row padding: **+{{ ((W.layout_factor.tp4-1)*100)|n(1) }}% streamed routed-expert bytes at TP4, +{{ ((W.layout_factor.tp8-1)*100)|n(1) }}% at TP8**; the shared expert's FP8 copy is read padded | safetensors headers (`data/checkpoint_manifest.csv`), `ops.rs::verify_head_fp8`, `packing.rs::sgl_expert_bytes`, `model.rs::sgl_init` |
| KV cache | main (compressed) KV **FP4** E2M1 + E4M3 scale per 16 ch; SWA KV FP8; indexer K FP4 | tech report §2.4.4, `inference/model.py` |
| kernels | hand-written CUDA for tcgen05: weight-streaming GEMV (`tcgemv*`), fused MoE (`tcmoe`, `sgl`), sparse attention, top-k, Mega-mHC (`hcpipe`), Markov draft head, Gumbel sampler. Every launch uses programmatic dependent launch (PDL); the indexer, compressor and mHC dot products run on side streams; the all-reduces (NVLS multimem + Lamport buffers) are pushed from the producing kernel. Our op graph counts about {{ w.kernels_per_step }} dependent kernel stages per step on the critical path (approximate) | `crates/kernels/cu/*.cu`, `model.rs` (`launch`, `par_fork`, `comm_ex`) |

